        "original_id": "130bd6cc-47df-54b0-a989-092e7a3a72d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brendan Bracken, Adolf Hitler, Winston Churchill\n- Organizations: Bank of England\n- Roles: British Conservative cabinet minister, central bank\n- Places: United Kingdom, Ireland\n- Topics: World War II, central banking\n\nFacts:\n- The Bank of England was established in 1694.\n- The Bank of England is formally named the Governor and Company of the Bank of England.\n- The Bank of England is the central bank of the United Kingdom.\n- The Bank of England is the second oldest central bank still operating, after the Sveriges Riksbank.\n- The Bank of England served as the model for most modern central banks.\n- Brendan Bracken was born in Ireland on 15 February 1901.\n- Brendan Bracken was a businessman and a minister in the British Conservative cabinet.\n- Brendan Bracken opposed the Bank of England's co-operation with Adolf Hitler.\n- Brendan Bracken later supported Winston Churchill's prosecution of World War II against Adolf Hitler.\n- Brendan Bracken died on 8 August 1958.",
